''Let's give you the latest on what's on our radar!''

----
'''It is always recommended that once a hotfix has been deployed to open the Area/Relic/Task interfaces.'''

It's been a jam-pact'd start to our sixth leagues! We've seen you running around Varlamore exploring new areas you've not seen properly or before, finally getting starting on your journey towards your ultimate bluetooth hally or pure tank builds and dodging the fires around the outskirts of Yama's lair in rhythmic fashion.

While this is just the beginning and we're excited to see what other amazing adventures you'll embark on this league, we've been contracted by Yama to make sure any outstanding issues are being looked into. And the team is hard at work to ensure we're keeping the league as smooth as possible (or forfeit our souls in the process) by combing through all of the issues and feedback you've raised.

This little update is to give you an idea of the things we're currently looking at and what sort of priority these things have on our lists. Please note that while we're trying to give you as much information as possible with what's on our radar, some things might take longer than expected to resolve, require a coldfix (game reboot) or be shifted to prioritise a newer and more severe issue.

We'll look to keep the list below up to date as best we can as issues are resolved. The best way to let us know of a problem is via the in-game 'Bug Report' function! Before we delve into the current roster, we've also got a few handy pieces of information that might just help with a few of the issues you may have experienced:

{{Collapsed section|18|PLAYER AWARENESS INFO}}
As we've seen some different interpretations "Whenever your combat spells Regenerate air runes, you have a 15% chance to restore 1 prayer point PER RUNE regenerated", we'd like to clarify:

* ''If 10 runes are regenerated, you'll gain 150% chance. This means you'll always get 1 Prayer Point and have a 50% chance to get another.''

If you have Barbarian Gathering and are struggling to complete any tasks that require you to equip a tool (i.e. 'Mine some Ore With a Steel Pickaxe'), try equipping the tool.

The Loot Tracker on RuneLite is currently counting 2 Implings being caught instead of one due to the loot multiplying. Players can right-click their butterfly net or magic butterfly net to open the impling tracker interface to check.

We'd recommend enabling back-to-back Hunter rumours if you're making use of so-called 'block lists' since the Hunters at the Hunters Guild will default to assigning you Jerboa if they aren't able to assign anything else (meaning if you can only obtain one rumour, complete that rumour and then ask for a new one, you won't be able to be assigned your desired rumour and will assign you Jerboa).

For players who have completed Death on the Isle and wondering where any items have gone, speak to the Head Butler once again to retrieve any items removed.
{{Collapsed section end}}

