{{Collapsed section|18|BEYOND LEAGUES VI {{!}} 29TH APRIL}}
While we've got a roster of fixes on our radar and set our priorities, this has meant that some issues you've raised won't be fixed within this League.

Rathering than leaving you to speculate, we'd rather be up front and set your expectations on what should be fixed. While this isn't the complete list, the issues below have been raised to be investigated for a future Leagues if we revisit those mechanics or features.

* The Shadowflame Quadrant isn't functioning as expected at the Doom of Mokhaiotl.
* Thorns don't work against Shades from the Shades of Mort'ton Minigame.
* Endless Harvest doesn't auto-move with Karambwanji or the Shark spot in Priffdinas.
* The Blue Moon Spear doesn't work with the 'Melee at Range' Pacts.
* Natures accord is failing to note Tree Roots.
* Loot from Master Farmers that goes into a Seed Box with Larcenist is not multiplied by 10x.
* While Wintertodt is covered by the drop rate modifier, it isn't covered by the 'Minigame' boost.
* Minion to have more customisable looting, such as clues and untradeables.
* The Clue Contract teleports a player to a tile they cannot move on for the 'Read "How to breed scorpions" By O.W.Thathurt.' Clue step.
* Thorns isn't triggering against an enemy attack that doesn't trigger a hitsplat.
* The Flask of Fervour isn't damaging certain enemies within the Chambers of Xeric.
* Blindbag is less effective with alot of movement, sometimes losing out on hits.
* Blindbag is removing offhand items with Kitted Scythes.
* If you have a Battleaxe in triggered with Blindbag, it stays equipped.

When it comes to the Demonic Pacts specifically, while we could spend the rest of the League tweaking and balancing Pacts to hopefully push those builds that feel weaker to a better place, the balancing of this particular system warrants plenty of time.

Touching on something we said previously, we don't want to spend the rest of the league 'chasing our tail' by constantly shifting the current balance of the Pacts. While not perfect, we think players are in a better spot with the extra resets and tasks we've added and we would hate to create any more 'pact regret'.

We really appreciate all the feedback and discussions we've seen around the new experimental system and we'll be looking to implement what we can if we are to revisit the Pacts in the future!
{{Collapsed section end}}

