{{Collapsed section|18|OUR PROPOSAL FOR PACTS {{!}} 20TH APRIL}}
We've seen plenty of you trying out our new take on the Combat Mastery system. With plenty of options and plenty of potential, we've already seen a huge roster of diversity when it comes to how you tackle combat. For starters, every pact has been chosen at least once but with countless potential builds - we've not even scratched the surface!

While there has been plenty of fun, we are also very aware of your feedback regarding the Demonic Pacts system. This morning, the team got together and we are proposing some changes to make this a bit nicer for everyone!

===Resets===
First up, we know there has been a bunch of feedback around resets. Not only just the amount available but also how you acquire them. This can feel like quite a hefty ask for a player to undertake, especially when it comes to more casual players and those unfamiliar with similar systems.

The current system allows for 3 full resets (a total of 4 builds) with each reset coming from your first 3 unique Echo Boss kills. We always wanted this system to feel meaningful and not trivialise your progression or level of power. Although from a player’s perspective, when compared to previous Leagues and especially Grid Master it is much slower, even if intentional. This was mainly to slow down the progress compared to the pace that shot up from Leagues V and would allow more time for players to explore Varlamore, a fresh area to lots of players!

While these design goals are still something we want to keep for this league, it is also important for us to ensure the system still feels fun. So, for our first change, you may have seen that '''Yama has been truly kind and given everyone a reset for no extra cost!''' While this is free, it should still be used wisely!

Secondly for later this week, we are also going to '''give another unlockable reset.''' This one will be everyone's first 'extra' reset as we're adding this onto the 'Defeat Hueycoatl 1 Time' task. Anyone that has already done this task will have the reset added after this week's game update.

===Neutral Pacts===
Another big piece of feedback we have seen is in the power of the neutral pacts not feeling strong enough to be effective. Especially when it comes to fighting specific bosses with a high defence in X style or protection against said style, can make it feel more difficult than powerful.

To combat this, we are looking to make the following changes to the neutral pacts:

* Increase Prayer Penetration pacts from 15% to '''25%.'''
* Increase small accuracy pacts from 15% to '''25%''' & big accuracy pacts from 35% to '''50%.'''
* Include '''an additional 10% accuracy''' to all +1% damage pacts. 

We feel these buffs will make a significant enough impact to ensure that all builds are gaining a meaningful difference where it matters most. This means that with 1 big accuracy pact, 3 smaller accuracy pacts and 2 damage pacts, you'd be gaining and additional +65% more accuracy (or +145% total compared to the previous +80%)! Being able to actually hit the boss should help a lot more when you've picked a build that isn't too good against certain NPCs.

You'll see these changes come with this week's game update.

===Echo Bosses===
Next on our list is those demonic looking baddies. In the same vein as the above feedback point, some builds just feel incredibly weak against certain bosses, which can feel bad when you've been working towards a specific style for the last 20 hours.

The team are going to look at all Echo Bosses across the board and balance the most egregious outliers to make sure that all builds have a decent chance against these bosses. This also mean we'll be investigating reports of thorns not working correctly against Echo Bosses and checking Mage & Range pacts inside the gauntlet too.

While we cannot give you all of the specifics just yet we can at least let you know how we're changing '''Echo Amoxliatl:'''

* Range Defence lowered from 200 to '''40'''
* Magic Defence lowered from 100 to '''20'''

Keep an eye out for more information once we've finalised the specific changes!

===Point Tasks===
Another thing the team would like to explore is how players acquire Pact Points. As it can take a handful of points to start truly seeing the power and benefit of the Demonic Pacts, the current roster of tasks makes it difficult to get a good head start in your build, meaning the power comes much later than most would like.

With this is mind, the team ''would like'' to see if there are some 'better' ways of getting points earlier. There's a few options we could go down here, whether this is replacing some tasks with others, adding additional ones or something in between. If the team look to change anything here, one thing we will not be doing is increasing the total amount of points you'll be able to get, so you'll still have 40 max regardless of how we progress.

The team are open to hear your thoughts on which direction we should go but please note that if we proceed with these changes they won't be available until at least next week's game update.

===Closing Words===
While we've seen other feedback regarding specific builds and their power, we don't want to jump the gun too early and end up chasing our own tail. Instead, we would rather start by making more meaningful, widespread changes to fix those issues first, before diving into any specific and consistent problems.

The team will continue to monitor the Demonic Pacts very closely and make any necessary changes after the above fixes have been implemented. It's important to us the spirit of the system and this league remains but without compromising the fun and freedom of this new system.

Alongside these changes, we'll still be keeping this newspost up to date with all of the known issues and when they have been fixed, so bookmark this page for all the latest. This week's update will also be happening on Thursday instead of Wednesday this week. This will be at the regular time with the regular downtime, just a day later.

Thank you all for letting us experiment with something brand new and happy 'scaping!
{{Collapsed section end}}

